## Testing instructions

### Quick UI check (browser console)

The fastest way to verify the link insertion and modal without doing a real plugin update. On `wp-admin/plugins.php`, open DevTools and paste:

```js
(() => {
    const slug = wcStripePluginsPageParams.plugin_slug;

    // Insert a fake "Updated!" row right after the Stripe plugin row.
    const pluginRow = document.querySelector(`tr[data-slug="${slug}"]`);
    if (!pluginRow) { console.warn('Stripe plugin row not found'); return; }

    // Mirror what `wp.updates.updatePluginSuccess` does to the plugin row,
    // otherwise the row keeps its `.active` bottom box-shadow and the preview
    // shows a stray 1px line above the green notice that doesn't appear in
    // real updates.
    pluginRow.classList.remove('update');
    pluginRow.classList.add('updated');

    const fakeRow = document.createElement('tr');
    fakeRow.className = 'plugin-update-tr active updated';
    fakeRow.dataset.slug = slug;
    fakeRow.innerHTML = `
        <td colspan="4" class="plugin-update colspanchange">
            <div class="update-message notice inline updated-message notice-success notice-alt">
                <p>Updated!</p>
            </div>
        </td>`;
    pluginRow.after(fakeRow);

    // Fire the same event WP fires after a successful update.
    jQuery(document).trigger('wp-plugin-update-success', [{ slug }]);
})();
```

Expected:

- The fake row reads `Updated! See what's new`.
- Clicking the link opens the WordPress plugin information modal directly on the **Changelog** tab (no page navigation).

### End-to-end (real update flow)

1. Make sure an update is available for this plugin on the Plugins page. The simplest way is to lower the `Version:` header in `woocommerce-gateway-stripe.php` (e.g. set it to `8.0.0`), then hit **Check again** on the Updates page so WordPress detects a newer version on wp.org.
2. Go to `wp-admin/plugins.php`.
3. In the WooCommerce Stripe Gateway row, click the inline **update now** link.
4. Wait for the row's status to flip to **Updated!**.
5. Verify the message now reads: `Updated! See what's new`.
6. Click the appended link — the modal should open on the **Changelog** tab.
7. Trigger an update for any other plugin and verify the link is **not** appended to its `Updated!` notice.

### Automated checks

- `npm run test:js -- --testPathPattern=plugins-page` (11 specs pass)
- `npm run test:php -- --filter WC_Stripe_Plugins_Page_Controller_Test` (5 specs pass)

